  "worked_solution": "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n|u\\cdot v|\\le \u2016u\u2016\\cdot \u2016v\u2016.\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $\u2016u\u2016.$ So first, we compute $\u2016u\u2016$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016u\u2016 & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{k})^{2}+(-\\sqrt{k})^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2+2k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le \u2016u\u2016\\cdot \u2016v\u2016 \\\\ |-2| & \\le \\sqrt{2+2k}\\cdot (1) \\\\ 2 & \\le \\sqrt{2+2k} \\\\ {2}^{2} & \\le {(\\sqrt{2+2k})}^{2} \\\\ 4 & \\le 2+2k \\\\ 2 & \\le 2k \\\\ k & \\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $1.$",
